Fix null-pointer dereference in ALTREP_UNSERIALIZE_EX on a malformed
serialized ALTREP class descriptor.

A crafted serialized stream that presents an ALTREP object whose class
descriptor is not a well-formed three-element pairlist crashes R while
unserializing it:

    ==1==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: SEGV on unknown address
    READ of size 8
        #0 CHK                    src/main/memory.c:160
        #1 CADDR                  src/main/memory.c:4496
        #2 ALTREP_UNSERIALIZE_EX  src/main/altrep.c:303
        #3 ReadItem               src/main/serialize.c:1922
        #4 R_Unserialize          src/main/serialize.c:2294

ReadItem() reads the descriptor (info) from the stream as an arbitrary
object and hands it straight to ALTREP_UNSERIALIZE_EX(), which reads
CAR(info), CADR(info) and INTEGER0(CADDR(info))[0] with no validation.
On the serialize side that descriptor is always list3(csym, psym,
stype) -- a three-element pairlist whose third element is an integer
scalar -- but a hand-crafted stream can supply a shorter list, a
non-list, or a third element that is not an integer vector, so CADR /
CADDR walk off the end of the list and dereference an invalid pointer.

ALTREP_UNSERIALIZE_CLASS() already guards its own reads with
"TYPEOF(info) == LISTSXP", but ALTREP_UNSERIALIZE_EX() reads the fields
before calling it, and that guard alone would not catch a list shorter
than three elements or a wrong-typed type field.

Validate the descriptor up front and reject a malformed one with the
same error the function already raises for an unusable descriptor
("cannot unserialize this ALTREP object").  The checks are staged so
each CDR/CDDR/CADDR is reached only after the preceding node is known to
be a pairlist, so the validation itself never dereferences off the end.

unserialize() of untrusted data is documented as unsafe, but a hard SEGV
rather than a clean R error is still a robustness bug.  Reachable from R
via unserialize() / readRDS() on an attacker-supplied stream.

Found by fuzzing R with libFuzzer + AddressSanitizer.

Upstream status: NOT YET REPORTED to the R Bugzilla as of 2026-08-10.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/altrep.c
+++ b/src/main/altrep.c
@@ -298,6 +298,19 @@
 attribute_hidden SEXP
 ALTREP_UNSERIALIZE_EX(SEXP info, SEXP state, SEXP attr, int objf, int levs)
 {
+    /* info is the serialized class descriptor: a three-element pairlist of
+       the class symbol, the package symbol, and an integer scalar type
+       (see SET_ALTREP_CLASS_SERIALIZED_CLASS / list3 above).  A crafted
+       serialized stream can put any object here, so reject a malformed
+       descriptor with a clean error rather than dereferencing CADR/CADDR
+       off the end of a short or wrong-typed list. */
+    if (TYPEOF(info) != LISTSXP ||
+	TYPEOF(CDR(info)) != LISTSXP ||
+	TYPEOF(CDDR(info)) != LISTSXP ||
+	TYPEOF(CADDR(info)) != INTSXP ||
+	XLENGTH(CADDR(info)) < 1)
+	error("cannot unserialize this ALTREP object");
+
     SEXP csym = ALTREP_SERIALIZED_CLASS_CLSSYM(info);
     SEXP psym = ALTREP_SERIALIZED_CLASS_PKGSYM(info);
     int type = ALTREP_SERIALIZED_CLASS_TYPE(info);
